WEBVTT

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:13.640
Kono basho wo dete aruku
<i>Walking out from this place</i>

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:18.210
Michi no koto wo kangaeru
<i>Pondering the path</i>

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:22.650
Sora wa mada hayai yuugata
<i>The sky is still early dusk</i>

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:28.350
Kumo ni iro wo nokoshite
<i>Leaving twilight colors on clouds</i>

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.440
Hajime mo owari mo iranakatta
<i>I didn't need a beginning or an ending</i>

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.570
Kimi no me ga tsubuyaita
<i>Your eyes murmured to me</i>

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:48.940
Donna kioku wo sagashitara
<i>What memory do I need to search...</i>

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:53.420
Mune no fukami e todoku no darou
<i>... in order to reach deep into my heart?</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:57.650
Nagasugita kimi no iu...
<i>The too long days you speak of...</i>

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:02.290
...hibi wa hitoyo no yume no you de
<i>... are like a one night dream</i>

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:06.530
Owaru koto ga shinjirarenai
<i>Not able to believe it will end</i>

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:11.470
Mezameno toki wa mada tooi
<i>The time to awake is still far away</i>

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:19.930
Sen no yoru wo kesenaide
<i>Don't erase a thousand nights...</i>

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:26.080
Mada koko wo tatenai
<i>Still can't depart from here</i>

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.830
Yuki.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:55.170
Are you going somewhere?

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.230
Huh? Yeah.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.180
What are you upset about?

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.740
Nothing.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.840
Knock it off.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:09.860
Mom and Dad were so against it...

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:12.220
...but the moment they found out
they were going to be grandparents...

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:15.290
...they talk about nothing
but Miho. Where do I stand?

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.300
Hey, I gave up on becoming an actor and
took over the family business, you know.

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:21.340
You wouldn't have been able
to get married if you hadn't.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:24.970
Hey...

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:28.300
Tell HER that I won't need supper.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:29.900
Yuki!

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:32.850
Stupid. You should be ashamed.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:41.610
I'm still in Tokyo. Yeah.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:46.130
Is it okay if I'm a little
late for our meeting?

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.720
Yes. There's a place
I've gotta go to.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:52.290
Give me two hours,
to be safe. Sorry, thanks.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:55.360
Yeesh. Oh, okay.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.200
You owe me one.

00:02:58.270 --> 00:02:59.740
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:07.410
Two hours?!

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.850
- Hurry!
- Wait!

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:58.500
Capricious Unending Corridor

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:04.340
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.860
<i>Here.</i>

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.180
I really did hear it.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:51.180
I'm not doubting you, but
that's just hard to believe.

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:57.080
Yes, the library's search engine
is linked on-line, but...

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:00.420
More importantly, do you think
you can find anything on your end?

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:03.090
<i>I'm... about to start digging.</i>

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:05.900
If there is some
thing in "The World"...

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:11.060
...I think it was already inside
the previous version, "Fragment."

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:16.340
I bet CC Corp. put it on the
market without knowing about it.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:21.510
If they had known, I'm sure even they
wouldn't have sold something so dangerous.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:26.950
If that's the case, the developer
of"Fragment" holds the key.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:28.990
He must have something...

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:34.590
<i>Mr. Tokuoka, what is it?</i>

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:36.560
<i>What's wrong? Mr. Tokuoka!</i>

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:41.040
Mr. Tokuoka...

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:48.110
What's that all about?

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:02.050
<i>We are checking into the
cause. Please stand by.</i>

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:05.090
Oh...

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:16.600
<i>We're sorry, but for your safety,
please leave the building momentarily.</i>

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:19.730
<i>We will give you directions,
so please follow them calmly.</i>

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:47.430
Please don't use the escalator!

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.160
Hey, stop pushing me!

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:50.500
Please don't run!

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:51.540
Oh.

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:56.480
You cannot use the escalator!
Please follow instructions!

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:13.530
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:17.990
A in C major... A disruption
in communication, and now...

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:23.870
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:26.670
No way. Couldn't be.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:44.490
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:46.290
Oh, really?

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:55.240
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.200
Okay then...

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:04.750
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:07.270
This way! This way, hurry!

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:13.420
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:16.320
Please proceed slowly without pushing!

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:21.930
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:23.900
Hey, that's the opposite direction.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:26.070
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:27.800
I wouldn't go if I were you.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:28.600
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:30.760
There are shutters inside there, too.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:30.840
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:33.810
Even if you go through there,
you can't get out of the building.

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:40.750
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:44.810
Why? Why are you
so sure of yourself?

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:47.860
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:50.550
Who are you?

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:50.930
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:55.020
I work on the upper floor.
This way.

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:56.030
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:57.660
Hey...

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:18.350
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:21.290
What rotten luck. We would have
been able to get out no problem...

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:21.360
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.760
...had we been on the
first or second floor.

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:23.820
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:26.620
The automatic door won't
open if the power's out.

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:26.690
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:27.790
We can break the glass.
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:27.860
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:31.460
That's thick, reinforced glass.
I don't know how strong it is...
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:31.530
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:33.730
...but do you think
it will be that easy?

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:35.440
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:38.840
The door may be reinforced,
but the 1 st floor store windows...

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:38.910
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:41.880
...facing the roadway, and
the 2nd floor store windows...

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:41.940
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:44.970
...facing the balcony should be
normal glass, don't you think?

00:09:44.970 --> 00:10:00.430
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:02.660
See, it won't open.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:02.730
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:04.700
Do you think I screwed up?

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:05.870
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.490
Not really.

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:08.340
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:11.640
The ones who went down
the escalator are hopeless.

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:12.510
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:17.710
It's like being inside a huge tube.
There are too many people to fit at once.

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:17.780
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:22.220
If their anxiety and fear pass the
breaking point, mass panic will erupt.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:22.280
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:26.080
I don't want to be in the middle
of a bunch of people freaking out.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:26.490
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:29.420
Same here.
I want no part of it.

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:29.890
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:32.920
If so, we have to
think of another way.

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:35.200
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:38.430
Can't we just wait it out?

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:38.830
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:41.230
Okay, why don't you
call on your cell for help?

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:41.300
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:43.570
Oh! I totally forgot about that!

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:48.440
Phone: NO SERVICE

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:49.670
Oh...

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:52.650
I don't think you should
expect help from outside.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:53.680
Huh?

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:57.450
The computers above are connected
to the servers at the main office...

00:10:57.520 --> 00:10:59.820
...but they went down a moment
before the alarms went off.

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:02.650
And, taking the unusable cell
phones into consideration...

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:05.850
...I have a feeling this may
be more than just our problem.

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:17.300
This way, this way.

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:24.910
Lift the other side.

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:31.480
Say, is the net causing all this?

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:34.940
I guess you're not a complete idiot.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:36.420
Hey.

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:38.950
Okay. Let go.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:08.620
Phone: NOT IN SERVICE

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:10.420
Damn.

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:19.960
I don't want juice!
Give me info, dammit!

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:27.300
Do you know a lot about the net?

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:29.310
I only poke around it
blindly now and then...

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:32.240
...so I can't say I know
a lot about it. Why do you ask?

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:34.940
Before this happened,
I saw a field from a game...

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:39.850
...flash on a movie screen only for
a second. I thought it was strange.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:51.190
It's the age where even
cinema feed is being streamed.

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:53.500
But don't you think that's strange?

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:57.770
That name of that
particular game is "The World"...

00:12:57.840 --> 00:13:02.240
...and there's a lot of rumors that it's
infected by viruses and other things...

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:05.440
Urban myths?

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.140
No!

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:11.480
Actually, a friend of mine went
into a coma while playing the game...

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:14.890
Do you smell something burning?

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:35.840
Those idiots. Turn off the
oven before running away.

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:37.430
Maybe we should hurry.

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:38.380
What?

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:42.070
Have you forgotten?
The first floor is Food World.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:46.850
I told you. We could get out easily
if we were on the 1 st or 2nd floor.

00:13:46.920 --> 00:13:49.450
But now that the downstairs is
abandoned, and if more ovens...

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:51.920
...have been left on,
in the worst-case scenario...

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:55.430
...a real fire would break out.
And one other thing...

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:58.060
Don't say it.
I don't want to hear.

00:13:58.130 --> 00:14:00.830
I know now we should hurry.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:02.990
Okay, then I won't tell you.

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:16.070
Harald... The Epitaph of...

00:14:19.990 --> 00:14:21.960
This is him?

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:29.160
Phone: Incoming message: Kyo

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:38.260
Now!

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:43.910
I guess we'll find out what floor
it's stopped at when we open it.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.080
Yeah.

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:49.380
Here goes!

00:14:56.990 --> 00:14:58.960
The nonstop express!

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:13.700
Great, we're through.

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:16.940
Uh, how do you do.
My name is Mai.

00:15:17.010 --> 00:15:19.740
The hellos aren't that important.
Where's Yukichin? Is she all right?

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:25.280
I saw on the news that something crazy is
happening in Yokohama. Isn't she with you?

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:30.050
I was looking up something in Tokyo
and Mr. Tokuoka is heading over there...

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:32.680
...but I can't reach him
on his cell phone.

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:35.160
Something crazy? What happened?!

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:40.130
I don't know. I phoned to
find that out, but never mind.

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:44.830
Would you keep trying to contact
Mr. Tokuoka? I'll hunt down Yukichin.

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:46.530
Sure.

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:52.010
Phone: Calling: Mr. Tokuoka

00:15:54.750 --> 00:15:57.720
<i>The phone you are trying to reach
is either out of the coverage area...</i>

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:09.060
Phone: Traffic stopped into Yokohama,
Sakuragi Town and a part of Keihin area.

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.430
Phone: All thoroughfare
stopped for J R Rail...

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.700
Phone: ...Tokyo Express, Keiyo Line,
Keihin Express, and the subway.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.570
Phone: Outbreak of fires
through parts of the city.

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:23.100
They say that Yokohama has
been attacked by city guerrillas.

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:24.040
Terrorists?

00:16:24.110 --> 00:16:27.140
I don't know, but it's sure been
severed from the rest of the country.

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:38.520
Of course, you're the one
who will decide what to do...

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:42.150
...but just waiting doesn't
present much of a future.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:44.660
If you want to die here,
that's your life.

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:48.260
You're kidding.
Is it really that bad?

00:16:48.700 --> 00:16:50.860
That's how <i>I see it.</i>

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:55.200
But why?
How did this happen?

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:59.110
If we die here, we won't be able
to search for an answer to that.

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:02.880
That's too much to deal with.
I can't understand.

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:05.610
Take a look.

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:12.620
An actual fire breaks out.
The system malfunctions.

00:17:12.690 --> 00:17:17.220
Or, an air conditioner with a temper
blows out hot air somewhere.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:19.660
That's when that'll turn on.

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:22.530
If a large quantity of
carbon dioxide is expelled...

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:24.070
...what do you think will happen?

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:25.870
Anoxia, suffocation...

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:27.600
I don't like the idea of that.

00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:31.170
Wait. Then what about the
people on the escalator?

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:34.040
I guess all we can
do is pray for them.

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:36.210
That's cruel!

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.220
You're a good girl, aren't you?

00:17:39.790 --> 00:17:42.980
Everyone loves you and
you're an honor student...

00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:46.150
Maybe you're trying to be
bad and used a swear word...

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:49.250
...but that's as far as you
can go. Neither good nor bad...

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:51.300
That's not...

00:17:51.370 --> 00:17:56.130
What the hell can we do
when we're in danger ourselves?

00:17:56.940 --> 00:17:59.910
If we could just tell them that
there's an escape route here...

00:18:02.410 --> 00:18:05.110
I won't stop you. If that's
what you want to do, then do it.

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:09.120
But I'm going.
One more thing...

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:11.980
Glass will break,
but acrylic won't.

00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:13.980
Acrylic?

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:26.590
If that's true...

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:28.900
If that's true, there's no way
I can turn my back on them!

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:58.560
Let go! Don't worry about me!

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:07.470
Okay!

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:10.540
Quickly!

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:26.760
Don't look down!

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:39.770
Did you get a hold of him?

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:40.770
Not yet.

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:41.540
I see...

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:44.810
Say, do you think I
should go to Yokohama, too?

00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:46.240
No.

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:47.210
But, I...

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:50.180
I don't want to lose
contact with you, too.

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:52.580
They're both okay, aren't they?

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:54.120
Yeah.

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:07.960
Are you okay?

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:13.870
Ouch!

00:20:16.640 --> 00:20:18.610
I think I twisted my ankle...

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:27.110
These sure are thick.

00:20:29.360 --> 00:20:30.950
Why don't you wear contacts?

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:33.360
My eyes are very
sensitive to them.

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:34.690
Do they get bloodshot?

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:36.520
Yeah.

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:38.530
So you're having hard
times with many things.

00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:04.160
I guess the escape plan
is a success.

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:06.750
Wow...

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:43.290
It's like the world has ended.
What happened to make it this way?

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:45.390
The second coming of Pluto's Kiss.

00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:49.200
When computers abandon us,
there's really nothing to it.

00:21:50.440 --> 00:21:51.870
Where are you going?

00:21:51.940 --> 00:21:53.930
Home.

00:21:54.010 --> 00:21:57.140
Oh, yeah. That was a lie.

00:21:58.280 --> 00:22:01.610
The escalator isn't
surrounded by acrylic.

00:22:01.680 --> 00:22:05.310
I wanted to tease you,
so I made it up.

00:22:05.390 --> 00:22:08.380
So, those people
are fine, probably.

00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:10.360
Sorry for tricking you.

00:22:10.420 --> 00:22:12.090
But why?

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:15.320
Your last name
is Aihara, right?

00:22:17.030 --> 00:22:19.560
Have we met somewhere before?

00:22:19.630 --> 00:22:22.470
Yeah, at Miho's wedding.
For one thing...

00:22:22.540 --> 00:22:27.840
...you weren't wearing glasses then,
so you probably didn't see my face.

00:22:27.910 --> 00:22:31.540
That little... Are you
a friend of my sister's?

00:22:31.610 --> 00:22:33.310
You could say that.

00:22:33.380 --> 00:22:35.410
Is that why you helped me?

00:22:35.480 --> 00:22:38.920
Good question. I didn't
really intend to help you.

00:22:38.990 --> 00:22:42.320
If it bothers you, think of me
as someone you just bumped into.

00:22:42.390 --> 00:22:45.880
Well, sorry, but this is the
last time we'll see each other.

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:50.090
Looking at you reminds me of
my old self and it embarrasses me.

00:22:55.000 --> 00:22:56.940
And this may be
none of my business...

00:22:57.000 --> 00:22:59.800
...but keep the glasses on.
They look good on you.

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:26.130
Damn!

00:23:55.100 --> 00:23:56.790
Yukichin?

00:23:57.630 --> 00:23:59.160
Mr. Tokuoka?

00:23:59.230 --> 00:24:00.860
Thank god...

00:24:03.700 --> 00:24:07.610
Don't "Thank god" me.
You're six hours late!

00:24:08.140 --> 00:24:11.510
I'm sorry, forgive me.
But I had trouble, too, y'know...

00:24:11.580 --> 00:24:15.110
Uh, well, never mind that. By chance,
have you been waiting the entire time?

00:24:15.180 --> 00:24:19.740
I thought of going home,
but a lot happened...

00:24:19.820 --> 00:24:21.620
A lot.

00:24:21.690 --> 00:24:23.550
- Like what?
- This.

00:24:29.260 --> 00:24:31.890
Does this have something
to do with "The World"?

00:24:33.530 --> 00:24:35.930
Well, I hope not. But...

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:39.490
Still almost no one
realizes anything, huh?

00:24:39.570 --> 00:24:40.630
Yeah...

00:24:40.710 --> 00:24:44.610
Now that I'm aware of it,
what should I do?

00:24:44.680 --> 00:24:46.810
Can I count on your help?

00:24:48.180 --> 00:24:49.670
Yeah.

00:25:05.830 --> 00:25:08.490
Yeah! I'm fine.

00:25:08.570 --> 00:25:11.560
She's in front of me
right now. It's Mai.

00:25:11.640 --> 00:25:13.830
I have Kyo.

00:25:13.910 --> 00:25:16.140
Yeah, I know. Yeah.

00:25:16.210 --> 00:25:19.470
I'm okay, ma'am.
So, how'd it go?

00:25:19.550 --> 00:25:20.670
Huh?

00:25:20.750 --> 00:25:22.810
The Epitaph ofTwilight?

00:25:24.620 --> 00:25:26.110
What's that?

00:25:26.190 --> 00:25:28.150
The Epitaph ofTwilight...

00:25:29.060 --> 00:25:31.650
That's Kyo's territory.

00:25:32.230 --> 00:25:34.960
You said it was the background
prototype of"The World"...

00:25:35.030 --> 00:25:39.990
...is based on, right? The Epitaph
ofTwilight... That's what she says.

00:25:40.070 --> 00:25:43.000
By territory, you mean
she knows a lot about it?

00:25:43.070 --> 00:25:44.540
Yeah.

00:25:44.600 --> 00:25:49.130
All right!! Hey! We may have
caught the enemy by the tail.

00:25:50.080 --> 00:25:51.670
Really?!

00:25:51.750 --> 00:25:53.370
Yeah, probably!

00:25:53.450 --> 00:25:57.140
What's going on? Did
you hear what he just said?

00:25:57.820 --> 00:25:59.180
I heard it.

00:25:59.250 --> 00:26:00.620
<i>What does it mean?</i>

00:26:07.360 --> 00:26:09.790
Let me speak to Mr. Tokuoka.

00:26:15.870 --> 00:26:20.310
Tasogare no umi ni dete...
<i>Setting out in twilight seas...</i>

00:26:20.340 --> 00:26:25.250
Futari wa nidoto mou meguri...
<i>Will we never meet...</i>

00:26:25.250 --> 00:26:30.270
...aenaino?
<i>... again?</i>

00:26:36.960 --> 00:26:44.630
Kin no akari ga umi ni ochite...
<i>A light of gold falls into the sea...</i>

00:26:44.700 --> 00:26:49.760
...natsu no kaze ga togireta.
<i>... the wind of summer trails off.</i>

00:26:49.840 --> 00:26:55.140
Obieru futari ni tada...
<i>The frightened pair only hears the sound...</i>

00:26:55.210 --> 00:27:01.550
...yosetekaesu mizuoto.
<i>... of sea water coming and going again.</i>

00:27:02.920 --> 00:27:08.250
Donnani nami wo kasanete...
<i>No matter how I drown the waves...</i>

00:27:08.320 --> 00:27:13.620
Omoide wo sakendemo...
<i>Screaming out our memories...</i>

00:27:13.690 --> 00:27:18.790
Anata no ita kishibe niwa...
<i>I can never return to the shore...</i>

00:27:18.870 --> 00:27:24.740
...mou kaerenai.
<i>... where you were.</i>

00:27:25.140 --> 00:27:29.670
Tasogare dake wo daite.
<i>Embrace nothing but the twilight sky.</i>

00:27:29.740 --> 00:27:32.840
Ano hi no nami wa mou...
<i>The waves from that day are now...</i>

00:27:32.910 --> 00:27:36.710
...fukai umi no soko.
<i>... at the bottom of the deep ocean.</i>

00:27:36.780 --> 00:27:40.220
Kanashimi wo shiranai...
<i>They sleep as they embrace blue dreams...</i>

00:27:40.290 --> 00:27:45.590
...aoi yume wo mite nemutteiru.
<i>... that do not know sorrow.</i>
